Product config for fajita on OH 7.0 (the port's vendor repo has no 6.1 or 7.0 branch):
- add the parts OH 6.1+ requires that the 5.1 config lacks (rust_libc, skia, notofonts, alsa-lib, ... as in rk3568);
  7.0 also needs expat (xmp_toolkit_sdk) and vma, as rk3568 lists them
- 7.0 renames: the HDF device host is drivers_devhost (6.1: drivers_adapter); no qrcodegen (7.0 has
  qrcode_generator, which productdefine/common/inherit/rich.json already lists)
- drop init_feature_loader (unknown since 6.1) and wifi_feature_with_hdi_chip_supported=false (HalDeviceManager build error)
- Wi-Fi as on rk3568: the nl80211 wlan driver client, the default chip HAL (libwifi_hal_default) and the chip
  driver service (wifi_chip_device in device_info.hcs). Without the chip feature switch the Wi-Fi service needs
  chip_interface_service; 7.0's WifiTogglerManager gives up when it is missing and the service crashes at start
  (null WifiControllerMachine in ScanOnlyToggled), and Settings with it (isWiFiActive throws)
- power_suspend.json: no auto-suspend on screen timeout. Suspend makes dwc3 disconnect, which drops hdc
  (the port's USB_NOTES.md issue B1, route 1). The power key still suspends.

